# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (12 steps) =========================================================
info title=Ashfall
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A village on a volcanic table-land, buried to its eaves in grey ash - roofs, a bell house and a chapel spire sticking out of the drifts. The mayor's diary is scattered in five pages through the dug-out houses. Follow it to where the village went.
island on.arrive=message||A flat grey island, grey as a winter sky. Rooftops stick out of it in rows, and a little bell house, and a chapel's spire. No smoke from any chimney.

story ashshovel|Ash shovel|quest:Balboa_BrunosTool_Saw|A broad shovel from the tool shed, its blade worn bright.

note proclamation The last proclamation | (on the board at the bell house's foot)\n\nBY ORDER OF THE MAYOR\n\nThe ash is falling faster. Tonight, when the bell rings three times, everyone leaves for the safe house by the sea. Bring water and blankets. Leave the animals' doors open.\n\nDo not be afraid. We have done this before - a hundred years ago - and we came back.\n- Ilse Varga, Mayor
note page1 Mayor's diary, page one | Day 1. The mountain across the strait is coughing. Ash on the windowsills like flour. The children think it's snow.\nDay 3. It doesn't stop. The rats have come in from the fields into the town hall - they know something.
note page2 Mayor's diary, page two | Day 4. The baker kept baking. "People need bread," she said. The ash is up to the bakery's windows.\nDay 5. I found the old records: a hundred years ago they sheltered in the lava tube under the north cliff. There is a gate on it. The bell opened it then - three rings.
note toolbox Tool shed box | The tool shed's box, dug out from under the eaves: rope, nails - and a broad ash shovel, its blade worn bright. Somebody kept the school's path clear with it until the very end.
loot toolbox story:ashshovel*1;Rope*2;Nail*6
prop toolbox loot.refill=0
note page3 Mayor's diary, page three | Day 6. The school's door is buried. We dug the children out through the window, laughing as if it were a game. Mr. Brandt stayed to save the register.\nDay 7. Nobody will stay in the houses now.
note page4 Mayor's diary, page four | Day 8. Prayers in the chapel crypt. Beetles came out of the ash in the dark, big ones, and Father Okon chased them with a candlestick.\nDay 9. Tonight. I'll ring the bell myself.
note page5 Mayor's diary, page five | Day 9, night. Three rings. Everyone is going down the goat path to the sea with lanterns, a long line of lights. I'm the last. I'll leave this under the bell for whoever comes after.\n\nRing it three times. We'll be in the shelter, or long gone from it - either way, the gate will open for you.
note roll The shelter's roll | (chalked on a board inside the lava tube)\n\nTHE ROLL OF ASHFALL - ALL PRESENT\n\nVarga, Ilse (mayor). Brandt, Otto (teacher) and the register. Okon, Father. Kessler, Ana (baker) and bread. Thirty-one more names, every one ticked.\n\n(below, later:) The boat came on the fourteenth day. We have gone to the mainland. When the grass grows back, so will we.
note villagechest The village chest | The village chest, left in the shelter for whoever came: seeds to make the ash green, the plans for the terraced beds they'll need, salt meat, and the town's spare coin.
loot villagechest Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3*1;Seed_Grass*4;Seed_Pine*3;Cooked_GenericMeat*3;TradeToken*8
prop villagechest loot.refill=0
loot hallbox Plank*4;Rope*2;Plastic*2
prop hallbox loot.refill=0
loot bakerybox Cooked_GenericMeat*2;Raw_Potato*3
prop bakerybox loot.refill=0
loot jettybarrel Plank*5;Nail*6;Scrap*2
prop jettybarrel loot.refill=0
loot sunkcrate MetalOre*2;Scrap*2;Clay*2
prop sunkcrate loot.refill=0

prop schooldoor obj.name=schooldoor
prop schooldoor beh.use=Dig out the school's door
prop schooldoor beh.move=0,-3.2,0
prop schooldoor beh.moveTime=3
prop schooldoor beh.moveMode=switch
prop schooldoor if.use=has|story:ashshovel|1\nstate|schooldoor|closed
prop schooldoor on.use=message||You dig. The ash is packed hard as clay, then gives all at once - the school's door, open behind it.\nopen|schooldoor\nsound||event:/crafting/shovel_dig
prop schooldoor else.use=message||Ash packed solid in the doorway, up to the lintel. You'd need a shovel.
prop bell obj.name=bell
prop bell beh.use=Ring the bell three times
prop bell if.use=quest|9\n!signal|rung
prop bell on.use=message||One. Two. Three. The bell's voice goes out over the grey roofs - and far below, by the sea, something heavy grinds.\nsignal||rung\nopen|sheltergate\nshow|shelter\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell\nwait|1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell\nwait|1\nsound||event:/exploring/obstacles/bicyclebell
prop bell else.use=message||The village bell. The mayor rang it three times - read her pages first.
prop sheltergate obj.name=sheltergate
prop sheltergate beh.move=0,-12.8,0
prop sheltergate beh.moveTime=5
prop sheltergate beh.moveMode=switch
# (Utopia's entrance door as a ready piece wants Raft's entrance key and goes when used: this gate only sinks when the bell is rung - the ready piece's settings taken off)
prop sheltergate beh.use=
prop sheltergate if.use=
prop sheltergate else.use=
prop sheltergate on.use=

prop rooftops zone.id=rooftops
prop rooftops zone.radius=10
prop rooftops zone.message=The village square - or its roofs: grey drifts to the eaves, a bell house standing out of them, a board at its foot.
prop townhall zone.id=townhall
prop townhall zone.radius=3.5
prop townhall zone.repeat=never
prop townhall zone.message=The town hall, dim and grey inside - and full of rats.
prop rats creature.count=4
prop rats creature.respawn=0
prop rats creature.zone=townhall
prop school zone.id=school
prop school zone.radius=3
prop school zone.message=The schoolroom: little desks, a blackboard still chalked with sums, ash on everything.
prop chapel zone.id=chapel
prop chapel zone.radius=4
prop chapel zone.repeat=never
prop chapel zone.message=The chapel crypt - and something clicking in the dark. Beetles, the size of dogs!
prop beetles creature.count=3
prop beetles creature.size=1.3
prop beetles creature.respawn=0
prop beetles creature.zone=chapel
prop beetles tint.color=#4a4a48
prop beetles tint.amount=0.5
prop shelter obj.name=shelter
prop shelter beh.hidden=1
prop shelter zone.id=shelter
prop shelter zone.radius=4
prop shelter zone.message=The safe house: mattresses in rows, lanterns, water barrels, and a board covered in chalked names.
prop ashair atmo.fog=#6a6662
prop ashair atmo.fogAmount=0.25
prop ashair atmo.light=#b8b0a8
prop ashair atmo.lightAmount=0.2
prop ashair atmo.particles=mist
prop ashair zone.radius=40
prop cryptdark atmo.fog=#0a0806
prop cryptdark atmo.fogAmount=0.7
prop cryptdark atmo.light=#2a2218
prop cryptdark atmo.lightAmount=0.8
prop cryptdark zone.radius=7
prop hens creature.count=3
prop dolphins creature.count=2

quest title=Under the Ash
quest intro=A village buried in ash, and not a soul in it. A proclamation hangs at the foot of the bell house.
step reach|rooftops|1|Climb the road to the buried village
step read|The last proclamation|1|Read the mayor's last proclamation
step kill|Rat|4|Clear the rats out of the town hall
step pages||3|Find the mayor's first diary pages in the town hall and the bakery
step collect|story:ashshovel|1|Dig into the tool shed for a shovel
step reach|school|1|Dig out the school's door
step pages||6|Find the diary pages in the school and the chapel crypt
step kill|Roach|3|Fight off the ash beetles in the chapel crypt
step pages||7|Climb the bell house for the last page under the bell
step reach|shelter|1|Ring the bell three times and find the shelter by the sea
step read|The shelter's roll|1|Read the roll of names in the shelter
step open|The village chest|1|Open the village chest
quest done=Every name ticked. Ashfall got out - all of it - and left the door open for you. One day the grass will grow back, and so will they.
quest reward=Seed_Grass*4;Cooked_GenericMeat*2;Rope*3

save Ashfall
